       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen is double the maximum labeled daily dose. It carries a serious risk of GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm, and I'm not aware of any indication that supports it. The extra dose adds risk without added analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit, since the effect plateaus well below it.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n\n- **800 mg PO four times daily**, the maximum of 3,200 mg/day\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **A single 1,600 mg dose**, if that's what you meant, though that is also above the usual single-dose maximum of 800 mg\n\nIf you have a specific clinical reason for exceeding the maximum, such as a protocol or a specialist recommendation, please place it directly through your institution's process. That process should include pharmacy review and documented justification. I can also add a note to a lower-dose order if you want one."
